1
00:00:06,133 --> 00:00:08,056
I remember the feeling,

2
00:00:08,276 --> 00:00:10,358
warm but uneasy,

3
00:00:10,418 --> 00:00:12,481
new home, new city,

4
00:00:12,982 --> 00:00:14,824
low self-esteem.

5
00:00:14,844 --> 00:00:28,357
I took pill after pill

6
00:00:31,294 --> 00:00:43,050
just to quiet my head,

7
00:00:45,533 --> 00:00:49,259
then smoked by the window

8
00:00:49,715 --> 00:00:55,113
and stayed in my bed.

9
00:00:56,436 --> 00:01:01,995
Dropped acid alone while

10
00:01:02,869 --> 00:01:06,518
the ceiling turned strange

11
00:01:06,794 --> 00:01:12,538
and waited for something

12
00:01:13,911 --> 00:01:19,828
inside me to change.

13
00:01:21,474 --> 00:01:22,756
My dealer knew

14
00:01:22,816 --> 00:01:24,719
when I needed a spark,

15
00:01:26,128 --> 00:01:28,591
and I called that friendship

16
00:01:28,891 --> 00:01:38,310
because it was enough.

17
00:01:42,373 --> 00:01:52,595
At sixteen, I thought

18
00:01:52,716 --> 00:01:54,999
I had years left to lose.

19
00:01:55,141 --> 00:01:55,427
At seventeen,

20
00:01:55,499 --> 00:01:59,665
I had habits to choose.

21
00:01:59,690 --> 00:02:01,707
I don't miss the fear

22
00:02:01,928 --> 00:02:03,950
or the things I went through.

23
00:02:04,111 --> 00:02:06,313
I miss being young enough

24
00:02:06,414 --> 00:02:08,116
not to know what they'd do.

25
00:02:11,942 --> 00:02:13,744
My first love came

26
00:02:13,864 --> 00:02:16,227
through that apartment door.

27
00:02:16,667 --> 00:02:18,750
I had never let anyone

28
00:02:19,010 --> 00:02:20,732
that close before.

29
00:03:05,941 --> 00:03:43,993
I kept the opioids

30
00:03:44,013 --> 00:03:46,214
hidden where nobody would see,

31
00:03:46,234 --> 00:03:48,756
took more than I intended

32
00:03:48,836 --> 00:03:50,577
and kept it all with me.

33
00:03:50,597 --> 00:03:53,078
I overdosed in silence

34
00:03:53,138 --> 00:03:55,099
with the bedroom door shut tight,

35
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:57,461
then woke up hours later

36
00:03:57,561 --> 00:03:59,422
and said that I was alright.

37
00:04:00,082 --> 00:04:01,943
I didn't know what was wrong

38
00:04:02,263 --> 00:04:04,084
or why I hated my skin.

39
00:04:04,484 --> 00:04:06,445
I only knew the pills could cut

40
00:04:06,505 --> 00:04:08,185
the pressure down within.

41
00:04:28,332 --> 00:04:53,063
I don't call it good,

42
00:04:53,283 --> 00:04:55,224
and I don't call it bad.

43
00:04:55,364 --> 00:04:57,325
It held some of the worst

44
00:04:57,525 --> 00:04:59,546
and the best that I had.

45
00:04:59,626 --> 00:05:01,988
Now when I remember,

46
00:05:02,148 --> 00:05:03,829
I can't make it clean.

47
00:05:03,949 --> 00:05:05,870
I hated those years,

48
00:05:05,950 --> 00:05:08,071
but I still miss sixteen.

49
00:05:08,091 --> 00:05:10,072
Newark is traffic

50
00:05:10,412 --> 00:05:12,133
I pass on the way,

51
00:05:12,533 --> 00:05:14,354
but part of me stays

52
00:05:14,515 --> 00:05:16,436
in that bedroom some days.

53
00:05:26,160 --> 00:05:27,720
I wasn't chasing

54
00:05:27,820 --> 00:05:29,781
a story to tell.

55
00:05:30,421 --> 00:05:46,927
I don't miss that bedroom,

56
00:05:49,104 --> 00:05:55,460
at least not completely,

57
00:05:55,532 --> 00:05:57,571
but sometimes I miss

58
00:05:58,238 --> 00:06:05,472
what it meant to be sixteen.

59
00:06:06,691 --> 00:06:11,239
I remember the feeling,

60
00:06:11,299 --> 00:06:12,279
warm but uneasy,

61
00:06:12,319 --> 00:06:14,319
a new home, a new city,

62
00:06:14,359 --> 00:06:15,679
a life in between.
